# Error Handling — Bardak

## Target Pattern (implement when touching a feature)

### Failure Hierarchy (domain layer)

```dart
// lib/utils/failures/failure.dart
sealed class Failure {
  const Failure(this.message);
  final String message;
}

class NetworkFailure extends Failure {
  const NetworkFailure([super.message = 'Network error']);
}

class CacheFailure extends Failure {
  const CacheFailure([super.message = 'Cache read/write failed']);
}

class NotFoundFailure extends Failure {
  const NotFoundFailure([super.message = 'Resource not found']);
}
```

### Result Type (domain layer)

```dart
// lib/utils/result/result.dart
sealed class Result<T> {
  const Result();
}

class Success<T> extends Result<T> {
  const Success(this.value);
  final T value;
}

class Failure<T> extends Result<T> {
  const Failure(this.failure);
  final Failure failure;
}
```

### UseCase returns Result

```dart
class GetWordPacksUseCase {
  Future<Result<WordPackInfoResultEntity>> call(GetWordPacksParams p) async {
    try {
      return Success(await repository.getWordPacks(p));
    } on CacheException {
      return Failure(const CacheFailure());
    }
  }
}
```

### BLoC handles Result

```dart
Future<void> _onLoad(LoadWordPacks event, Emitter<WordPacksState> emit) async {
  final result = await getWordPacks(GetWordPacksParams(localeCode: event.locale));
  switch (result) {
    case Success(:final value):
      emit(WordPacksLoaded(packs: value.packs, locale: event.locale));
    case Failure(:final failure):
      emit(WordPacksError(failure: failure)); // typed, not raw string
  }
}
```

### UI maps Failure → localized message

```dart
// In widget, never in BLoC/state
String _failureMessage(BuildContext context, Failure failure) =>
    switch (failure) {
      NetworkFailure() => context.l10n.networkError,
      CacheFailure() => context.l10n.cacheError,
      _ => context.l10n.unknownError,
    };
```

## Current Gaps (fix incrementally)

| Issue | Location | Fix |
|-------|----------|-----|
| Raw `e.toString()` in state | `WordPacksNotCached.error` | Replace with `Failure` type |
| `try/catch Exception` swallowed | multiple BLoCs | Map to `Failure`, emit error state |
| `Future<bool>` from repo | `SettingsRepository` | Return `Result<void>` |
| `print()` in `AppBlocObserver` | `logging/` | Replace with `log()` from `dart:developer` |

## Rules

- Presentation MUST NOT catch raw exceptions from repositories.
- Error state fields MUST be typed `Failure`, not `String`.
- Data sources catch low-level exceptions and rethrow as domain exceptions
  (`CacheException`, `NetworkException`) which repositories map to `Failure`.
- Never use `dynamic` or `Object` as an error type in state.
